### TicketHub — manual API walkthrough
### Day 4: everything under /api/bookings now needs a JWT.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### ── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Log in as the seeded demo user (password: password123)
### Copy the `token` from the response into @token below.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@tickethub.dev",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Or register a new account
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "samridhi@tickethub.dev",
  "password": "password123",
  "displayName": "Samridhi"
}

@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 3. Check the token works
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. No token on a protected endpoint -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/bookings

### 5. Tampered token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.token

### 6. Wrong password -> 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
### (same error as an unknown email, on purpose)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@tickethub.dev",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### ── Public reads ────────────────────────────────────────────

### 7. Browsing events needs no token
GET {{host}}/api/events

### 8. Seat map, also public
GET {{host}}/api/events/1/seats

### ── Booking (authenticated) ─────────────────────────────────

### 9. Hold two seats. Note: no userId in the body any more —
### it comes from the token.
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [1, 2]
}

### 10. Same seats again -> 409, refused by the Redis claim
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [1, 2]
}

### 11. Overlapping request: seat 2 taken, so seat 3 must NOT be claimed
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [2, 3]
}

### 12. Confirm seat 3 was not partially claimed
GET {{host}}/api/events/1/seats

### ── Confirm with idempotency ────────────────────────────────

@holdId = PASTE_HOLD_ID_HERE
@idemKey = demo-key-001

### 13. Confirm
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{idemKey}}

{
  "holdId": "{{holdId}}"
}

### 14. Exact same request again -> same booking id, no second booking
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{idemKey}}

{
  "holdId": "{{holdId}}"
}

### 15. Same key, different body -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{idemKey}}

{
  "holdId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### 16. My bookings — scoped to the token's user
GET {{host}}/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── Cancel ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 17. Cancel booking 1
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18. Seats back to AVAILABLE
GET {{host}}/api/events/1/seats

### ── Error cases ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### Empty seat list -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": []
}

### Seat from another event -> 400 BAD_REQUEST
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [205]
}

### Unknown or expired hold -> 410 HOLD_EXPIRED
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "holdId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### Short password on register -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "short@tickethub.dev",
  "password": "abc",
  "displayName": "Short"
}
